[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Edgemodders/REDnode/main/native/redswap/nexus/brand/banner.png[/img][/center]

[center][size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Swap archives into the running game. See your new mesh, material or texture without a restart.[/color][/b][/size][/center]

[center][size=3]REDswap is a small RED4ext plugin for game version 2.5 that loads a changed .archive into Cyberpunk 2077 while you play. It is what REDnode uses for every archive swap, and any tool or script can call it.[/size][/center]

[center][size=3]What changed in each version: [url=https://github.com/Edgemodders/REDnode/blob/main/native/redswap/changelog.md]REDswap's changelog[/url] · Guide: [url=https://edgemodders.github.io/REDnode/redswap.html]REDswap docs[/url][/size][/center]

[line]

[quote][size=4][b][color=#fcee0a]STATUS: PREVIEW[/color][/b][/size]
Built in the open and tested in the game, on game version 2.5.
[b]Have REDnode?[/b] Then you have REDswap already: REDnode 0.41.0 and later install it. This page is for tools and players who want REDswap on its own.[/quote]
[line]

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]What it does[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Replaces an archive the game already loaded[/b], or [b]adds a new one[/b] to [i]archive/pc/mod[/i], in about 50 ms.[/*]
[*][b]Drops what the old archive held[/b] from the game's resource loader, so whatever loads it next gets your new version.[/*]
[*][b]ArchiveXL files too:[/b] .xl and .yaml files are swapped beside the archive, and ArchiveXL is asked to reload.[/*]
[*][b]Copies, never moves:[/b] the file you built stays where it is.[/*]
[/list]
With [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/35419]REDnode[/url], a swap also refreshes what is already in the world: the clothes V wears (Equipment-EX's slots included) and the inventory's preview of V, open or closed, with no button to press.

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Safe by design[/color][/b][/size]

Before it touches anything, REDswap checks the game:
[list]
[*]every game function it needs is in RED4ext's address list for your game version,[/*]
[*]the game's archive loader looks the way REDswap knows it,[/*]
[*]and the game's file cache holds each archive being replaced where expected.[/*]
[/list]
If any check fails, the swap is refused with a reason in [i]red4ext/logs/redswap-*.log[/i], instead of crashing the game. After a game patch, REDswap says it cannot swap until it is updated.

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Who it is for[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Modders[/b] who edit a mesh, material or texture and want to see it in the game at once: through [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/35419]REDnode[/url], its apps, or an AI assistant connected to REDnode.[/*]
[*][b]Tool makers:[/b] call [i]REDswap_Swap[/i] from redscript or your own RED4ext plugin. Examples are in the [url=https://edgemodders.github.io/REDnode/redswap.html]REDswap docs[/url].[/*]
[/list]
[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Requirements[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Cyberpunk 2077 on PC, game version 2.5.[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/2380]RED4ext[/url] 1.31 or later.[/*]
[*]Optional: ArchiveXL, for .xl and .yaml files.[/*]
[/list]
[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Install[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Vortex or EDGEdeck:[/b] Mod Manager Download, then enable and deploy.[/*]
[*][b]By hand:[/b] extract the zip into the game folder, so the plugin lands in [i]red4ext/plugins/REDswap/[/i].[/*]
[/list]
[b]With REDnode too:[/b] both carry the same files. If your mod manager shows a conflict, either copy works; let the newer one win.

[b]Uninstall:[/b] remove it in your mod manager, or delete [i]red4ext/plugins/REDswap/[/i]. REDnode needs it for archive swaps, so keep it if you use REDnode.

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]For tool makers[/color][/b][/size]

Three global functions, callable from redscript and from other plugins on the game thread:
[list]
[*][i]REDswap_Version() -> String[/i][/*]
[*][i]REDswap_Check() -> String[/i]: empty when REDswap can swap in this game, or why not.[/*]
[*][i]REDswap_Swap(files: String) -> String[/i]: absolute paths joined by "|"; answers JSON with what each file became.[/*]
[/list]
See [url=https://edgemodders.github.io/REDnode/redswap.html]the REDswap docs[/url] for examples in redscript, C++ and REDnode's JavaScript.

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Questions[/color][/b][/size]

[b]Do I need RED Hot Tools?[/b]
No. REDswap does the swap on game 2.5, where RED Hot Tools has no build yet. They can be installed together.

[b]My change does not show after a swap.[/b]
Things already in the world keep what they loaded. REDnode refreshes what V wears and nearby objects that use the swapped files; anything else shows once the game loads it again (walk away and back, or change the item).

[b]Can it swap sound?[/b]
Archives with the game's sound (.opuspak, .opusinfo) need more than a file swap. REDnode handles that around REDswap: use REDnode's archive swap for them.

[b]Is it free?[/b]
Yes, and open source under the MIT license, in [url=https://github.com/Edgemodders/REDnode/tree/main/native/redswap]REDnode's repo[/url].

